Uses `bit_cast(int, float64Val)` to read IEEE-754 bit patterns.  Under LP64 `int` is 64 bits so the bit_cast is valid; under --target arm32-baremetal `int` is 32 bits and `bit_cast(int, float64)` is an invalid LLVM cast (different bit widths).  Test logic is sound on both targets; the .bn just needs `bit_cast(int64, ...)` to be portable.  See claude-todo.md "TODO: substitute LP64-pinned conformance tests with target-aware variants" for the planned mechanism.
